**** UPGRADE STEP 1: You must run the new CatalogIndexMaker on all your
                     catalog files to create the Catalog.x.csum files.
                     If you have already done this, upgrade to a beta of 3.15
                     then it is not needed.

**** UPGRADE STEP 2: You must move the prompts.set file from the setup
                     directory to the Text directory, if you are using
                     different languages, you must have a copy of the
                     prompts.set file in every language sub directory of the
                     text directory.

**** UPGRADE STEP 3: All Arexx and Tempest Doors have changed.. all old
                     doors are no longer good.  You must be using only those
                     doors that are compabile with the new 3.15 format.
                     Many of you have already done this and are running 3.15
                     betas already, but for those just moving to 3.15 must
                     install only the 3.15 doors.  Can find an lha file with
                     all my new doors by typing UPDATE2 in doors area of my
                     bbs.

**** NOTE:  Hydracom made for Tempest is DIFFERENT than hydracom for amiga.
            The Hydracom that is online when you type UPDATE2 in the doors
            area is the CUSTOM version for Tempest bbs and goes in the
            tempest main directory. This custom version can not be used to
            call out with and you can not use the normal hydracom for amiga
            with tempest either.  The custom version I made is for Tempest
            only!  To actually use hydracom when you call around you must
            get the standard hydracom in my area 10 (Request)..


**** PROGRAMMERS NOTE: Tempest 3.15 changes all the door code for C
                       programming, as well as getvar variables for Arexx.
                       All doors must be converted to the new 3.15 format.
                       This will be the last time I change both...


- Bug Fix - Fixed bug in bbsconfig, where the system would crash if you tried
  to edit presets.
  (Thanks to The Minstrel for finding it)

- Bug Fix - Fixed small bug with a call to a routine, was passing information
  that it was not suppose to.

- Tempest now uses 20k less memory per node, when not in transfer.  There
  was a 20k buffer assigned for transfers and was being used even if the
  user was not trasnfering.  Now Tempest only assign's this memory if the
  user enters a file transfer, and returns the memory when they quit the
  transfer.

- Had to use dms instead of hschk for testing dms archives, hschk crashes
  on 040 with copy back on.  So I changed the ArcCheck.mod to use DmS.

  Also improved the bad archive testing, should detect all errors now.

- Activated the arexx command 'MayGetChar'... This arexx call checks to
  see if input has been made, and if not returns immediately.
  (Requested by Tas)

- Started compiling a special 040 version of the BBS Software.  I tried
  an 030 version but people complained of errors, so I dropped that one
  for now.. I think it had to do with certain 030 boards not the actual
  code to Tempest or anything.  But they can still use the regular
  68000 version with no problems.

- Added into the docs, info on changing the user activity in arexx.
  I had previously forgotten to add this into the docs.
  (Thanks to Tas for finding it)

- Added check sum files to the catalogs.  Must get the new
  CatalogIndexMaker util and run it once before running latest Tempest.

- Bug Fix - Fixed bug where a sysop could not copy / local upload files
  to an area that had a download only status.  The sysop should still be
  able to do those functions to an area with that status.
  (Thanks to Bluto for finding it)

- Bug Fix - Fixed bug with routine that loads the list of flagged files
  from a dropped carrier, I had some checking to make sure the flagged
  files were still online in the listing, It was not coded correctly
  (small mistake) so it was not working, now it will work.

- SERIOUS Bug Fix - Fixed new bug with Catalog.0 (Area 0's file listing)
  being deleted all the time!  Now File Mail catalog listing wont be
  deleted all the sudden.  This bug could possibly delete other area's
  catalog files too.  So make sure to update to this new version ASAP!

- Made it so a person could not select to resume an upload if it was already
  being uploaded on another node.

- Bug Fix - I found a bug in the new compiler SAS C 6.51 which was allowing
  duplicate uploads to happen on the bbs.  I worked around the compiler bug
  and now duplicates will no longer be possible.  I have already reported the
  bug to SAS C so hopefully next version will be fixed.

  * Feels good to report a bug to the actual compiler programmers.. hehe *

- Bug Fix - Finally fixed the Archive Checker Module so it will check zip
  files properly.  It requires ZIP to check the files.

- Bug Fixes - Fixed many small bugs related to the local uploading option
  in Tempest... Seems that the code was a complete jungle of jumps and it
  was not freeing memory or unlocking directories like it was suppose to.
  I think it is 100% now.  If anyone finds any problems please report them!
  (Thanks to Casa Nova for finding them)

- Bug Fix - When reading messages, if a message contained binary characters,
  the bbs would report over and over that the file contained binary chars.
  Now the bbs will report it once! and continue on with the display!
  (Thanks to Chad Kovac for reporting it)

- Bug Fix - Finally fixed the iconify hotkey/menu select item, before it was
  corupting things or crashing.  Now it works 1000% and fast!

- Bug Fix - Fixed small bug in file security, seems that if a file had
  sysop only status, the sysop could not access it, now they can!

- Added a total files/bytes selected and transfer time estimate for flagged
  files when you list your flagged files.

  <TOTALS>  Files: 1000  Bytes: 111,000,000  Transfer Time @ 115200 is 222:22

- Added an Iconify Gadget to the Un-Iconified screen.  If you click the close
  gadget in the upper left hand corner of the Un-Iconified Tempest screen the
  bbs will iconify, if the user is not in transfer.

- Added a Close Gadget to the User Status Window, so you can click the gadget
  to make the User Status Window go away.  Except when user is in transfer.

- Bug Fix - Fixed bug in BBSConfig in the definition of the presets.  The
  program was not passing some info properly and was disabling the ability
  to define presets.  Fixed
  (Thanks to Bandit and others for finding it)

- Bug Fix - Fixed bug when you edit a user's account while they are online,
  then hit 's' to save the account.. the 's' key would still be in the
  input buffer so it would enter the command 's' on the menu prompt the user
  was on when you exited the account editor.  Fixed now.
  (Thanks to Groovy for reporting it)

- Bug Fix - When you kill File Mail, the bbs should reflect the correct
  number of files waiting in file mail when you get back to the main
  prompt.
  (thanks to Chad Kovac and groovy for finding it)

- Many Bug Fixes - Fixed the bbs so if someone performs a function in the
  pull down menu they can not do another command in the pull down menu until
  they finish the one they have started.

  One exception to this however is the Enter/Exit chat, that one you can
  perform after entering it!

  Prevents things like editing user online over and over and over again.  I
  mean nobody would be crazy enough to do that, but just in case someone tries,
  it wont allow it.. It will however perform that task after you exit if you
  have entered a double command.. but at least there are no more crashes and
  problems with this!  Same goes for the next bug fix.

- Many Bug Fixes - Fixed it so if the sysop hits a function key, the bbs will
  not accept any other function keys to be hit until the current function
  is completed.
  (Thanks to Chad Kovac for reminding me to put those checks in.)

- Bug Fix - Fixed bug where you hit f7 to edit user online and you could not
  view that user's application.  Now you can!

- Bug Fix - Made Tempest auto load new prompts.set files if the language
  of a user logging on if their language is not the default.  After a user
  logs off, the bbs will reset the language file to the default language
  if the user was not using the default already.  So make sure the Default
  Language is the most Commonly used on your system.
  (Thanks to Groovy for reporting it)

- Re-Arranged the pull down menus again, now there are 3 menus:
  (System Menu, User Menu, Screen Menu)

- Noticed that the speed of the global area activation feature in the EAE util
  was very slow.  Re-worked the code and increased the speed!
  I also made it so the account would not be saved if there was no change
  needed, resulting in even more of a speed increase.

  Also fixed a bug where it would not let you edit an area that was turned off.

  Fixed possible problems with no error checking on input of choices. Now it
  checks to make sure the input is valid!

