- Added new Arexx Msg Port (not active yet), need ideas for commands.

- When you hit the HELP key to load your term program, the bbs node will
  iconify, since it is worthless to be un-iconified while you are in your
  term software.  I always found it to be a hassle to have to click pass
  that screen all the time!  Also saves chip memory.

- Bug Fix - Fixed a bug in the local uploader where it would get the
  filesize too soon, if you were still downloading a file that you are
  going to local upload, sometimes it was possible to have the filesize
  be smaller than the actual file.  Now Tempest grabs the filesize at
  the exact time you are typing descriptions.  Small change, but makes
  me happier.

- When you delete a user's account now, Tempest will check to see if
  there was an answers file found in the Accounts Applications direcotry.
  If it finds the file, it will prompt you asking if you would like to
  delete that file as well.  Helps keep the accounts dir cleaned up.

- Changed the ShutDown cli util to use msg ports instead of the old method.
  Should fix the random problems it was having.

- Tempest will now display the Doors Area & Bulletins Area Menus when you
  first enter the area.  After that first display, it will only show it again
  if you have expert mode off or if you enter the '?'.  But at least it will
  display it when you first enter, since most users don't memorize these
  commands and they are different on every single bbs.  Tempest still uses
  the expert mode flag for these areas, but will display the menu when you
  first enter.  Everyone should let me know how they feel about this.

- Bug Fix - I thought that the first time called variable was being set on
  users when they were new to the bbs for the first time, however it was not
  being set.  Fixed now.

- Fixed up the pull down menus a bit, they were not in line and so on, now
  they look and work better.

- Re-worked the door code some more.. were some small problems in the new
  door code that needed fixing..

- Added 3 more new C Door code commands: CopyFile, MoveFile, and FileSize.
  They are for copying, moving files, and getting the filesize of a file.
  Read docs for details.

- Bug Fix - Fixed small bug, when you had ansi off, was viewing an account
  in account editor, and viewed a user's application, ansi positioning
  would be messed up after viewing the application.  Fixed.

- Added new text file to the describe directory.  MsgPostInfo.x
  This new text file will be displayed (if exists) to user's just before
  entering a message on the bbs.  You can place message posting rules in this
  file or other information.  Rules such as what can / can't be posted or
  whatever you would like to place in it.  You can give it a .x (x=Area)
  extension, or you can place a .g extension for all areas.

- Bug Fix - Fixed the Text-MsgNextCaller display.  I had it using the
  languages.opt file, when in fact this text file should be fixed to one
  location only.  Now it is saved in the text dir root directory and ignore's
  all language sub-directories.
  (Thanks to groovy for reporting it)

- Added some color to the New User Questions, also re-arranged the wording
  and organization.  Much! nicer look and feel to it now.  Also easier for
  user's to understand.

- Bug Fix - Fixed 2 places where the bbs would not close the catalogs file
  after opening it.  This caused the file to be un-deletable until a reboot
  of the computer was done.

- Bug Fix - Fixed it so user's can reply to anonymous messages.
  (Thanks to Chad Kovac for reporting it)

- Added drop carrier checking to non stop message reading.

- Bug Fix - Fixed a bug when performing a download sysop, if you select a
  file that does not exist, the bbs would return wrong and kick the
  user off the bbs.. Fixed!

- Bug Fix - Found that, because of the way Tempest saves/reads messages,
  that when a user deleted messages, it was possible for the message base
  to get corupted if users on other nodes were saving/deleting messages at
  the same time.  This has been fixed now.  Hopefully this will solve alot
  of the problems!

- Bug Fix - Fixed arexx door command Getline / Hide.. Tas pointed it out to
  me that this input command should not show what is being inputed.  The
  whole idea of the hide option is so they dont see it.  So now it echo's
  dots when using this option.
  (Thanks to Tas for reporting it)

- Added new ~ Tilde code "Dump_File"  This one will display a text file
  without and ~ code detection and without pausing with More(y/n) prompts.
  (Thanks to Tas for Idea)

- Added a return to all arexx callers log entries.  I heard that arexx strips
  off any return's you add to the string so I made the arexx command just add
  one to whatever you send it.

- Added ability to change anonymous msg type in the Edit Header option.
  (Thanks to Night Stalker for coming up with idea)


  !!! Another World First on AMiga !!!

- Added Hydra Bi-Directional Protocol to Tempest!  Now you will be able to
  upload and download at the same time.  Tempest is the first in the WORLD!
  that has this on Amiga..




- Had to customize the hydra protocol to work with Tempest BBS.  Hydra did
  not work with BBS Software in its original state.

- Added upload/download protocol selection to the Terminal Settings for
  selecting between internal zmodem and hydra bi-directional protocols.

- Added upload/download protocol selection to the UserEditor.mod Module for
  selecting between internal zmodem and hydra bi-directional protocols.

- Added download list creation file for Hydra Protocol.

- Had to go back to the old SAS c 5.10 b compiler for now since there are
  some bugs in the new compiler.  Will go back to the new one once I work
  out some work arounds for the new compiler's bugs.  In doing this the
  exe size of tempest is around 60 k bigger.

- Bug Fix - Fixed a bug where memory was being over written, found this bug
  by switching back to the old Lattice Compiler for testing.

- Added support for Hydra uploads during a downloading.  Now after the download
  all files that were uploaded during the same time will be handled just like
  all uploads are handled.

- Added support for Hydra to handle the moving of completed uploads to the
  done directory.  Therefore handling all incomplete / complete uploads and
  allowing upload resuming.

- Added duplicate upload checking to Hydra Protocol, it will check the
  uploads.opt file as well as all other nodes for duplicates.  However it does
  not currently check the user's current file area's dir, unless you add it
  to the uploads.opt file, in which case it is fully working.

- Added support for Hydra so that all downloads are counted against users.
  Previously they were all free.  This is the last step in the instalation
  of hydra into Tempest.  Tempest now has it fully working and is the first
  in the world to support it on an Amiga bbs program.

- Added CPS and Transfer Time report to download status report in Tempest for
  Hydra protocol.  Now Hydra users can see their cps and transfer time for
  all downloads.

- Tempest no longer opens and closes the rexxsyslib.library everytime an arexx
  door is executed.  Now Tempest opens the library open loading tempest and
  closes it upon quiting tempest.  I also found out that Tempest was opening
  this library every time an arexx door was called and never closing it, just
  kept opening it.

- Had massive problems and bugs lately when I went back to sas 5.10b, so I
  went back to sas c 6.51, since the bugs on 6.51 are not as bad as 5.10b.

- Changed the last download/upload prompt to include an option to change
  protocol's just before starting a transfer.

- Added new feature for file areas.  Now it is possible to set up an area to
  not give uploaders any credits to any files uplaoded to that area.

